      "message": "This overwrites the device-specific `xdp_zc_max_segs` stored by `af_xdp_update_tx_max_segs()` during queue creation. Zero-copy devices with a limit below 18 will therefore still accept invalid chains and may lose completions/leak buffers. Could we initialize the copy-mode default before creating the queues, so a queried zero-copy limit is preserved?",
